# Panel 186 R7, lane land186, 2026-10-02: a group's record over a C union is
# built naming exactly one member of each union, so a construction may name
# fewer fields than the record declares, and `check` holds only its labels
# (`selfhost/check/group_fields.hero`); what it leaves out is `build`'s.
#
# A label naming no field is told as that, with the record's fields, and the
# field it may be is offered as a guess. R7's prototype told it *`SA` is built
# with every field, named: kind:, i:, f:, x:*, *all of them, always*, false of
# a group's record, and silent about the misspelling.

extern "ffi-a-construction.h"
    record SA
        kind: i32
        i: i32
        f: f32
        x: i32
    function sa_x(s: SA) -> i32

function main()
    b = SA(kind: 2, ff: 1.5, x: 4)  #~ wrong_label
    print(sa_x(b))
